Expected elements: present

All must-shows render: the exit ("← demo", x24) targets the chain, Call Trace and Event Log share one strip (y69-94) with Call Trace open, Values is a pane below the region (y566-895) and not a tab, and the DATA row sits inside the Transaction pane with no band above the identity bar.

Reproduction confirmed. Columns measure 683/454/287 (borders x4/686, x691/1144, x1149/1435; 4px gutters at x687-690 and x1145-1148), i.e. 1.337x/1.339x/1.335x the wide 913/608/383 against a viewport ratio of 1.333. The split is percentage-only: 47.7/31.7/20.0% at both sizes. The tabbed region is 240px empty (y321-560) of 492px inner = 48.8%; Values is 34px of 328px = 10.4%. Both standing numbers reproduce.

The wide prescription ("narrow the nav column") does NOT transfer: at 1440 that column is horizontally tight — row 4's label ends x1061 against opcode ink at x1060, and frame names and paths are ellipsised. The region has the wrong aspect, not simply too much width.

Change (b) is INERT here too — "COST · MANA" sets on one line, x1158-1235. (c) landed: "128 / 1,315" at x849-942. (a) is outside my lens.

On (d) I concur with the refutation and raise nothing: the vertical ramps (Code 19px against a 23px line pitch; Transaction 29px) each ghost exactly one partial line, which is the "more below" signal. The horizontal mask is a separate defect — finding 3.

Fixes: exclude the notice band from the content mask; let hash rows run full-pane-width.

Rating: 6/10

